# Flash bus mode for the LilyGo T-RGB envs (gm-2cl.19, 2026-09-08).
#
# The board file (boards/LilyGo-T-RGB.json) has said qio at 80 MHz all along,
# the flash is a Winbond W25Q128 with the quad eFuse set, and every build had
# been shipping IDF's default of dio because nothing carried the board's
# setting into the sdkconfig. A per-object LVGL draw profile of the
# new_profile page put 4 to 6 ms on every small widget while the draw calls
# themselves were 0.1 to 0.6 ms: the time is code and rodata fetched from
# flash on cache misses, and the flash bus is what sets it. In QIO the same
# widgets cost 2.1 ms and every page change drew 30 to 45 percent faster
# (tools/snapshot_lat.py, bench board, divider 8).
#
# The bootloader has to carry this too: it enables the chip's QE bit and sets
# the cache's SPI mode, while the image headers keep saying dio on purpose
# (IDF downgrades the header so esptool never programs a chip in a mode it
# cannot read). So a USB flash of bootloader.bin at 0x0 with the app is what
# switches a board; an OTA update alone leaves it in dio. /api/debug/flashmode
# reports the live mode.
#
# Chained after sdkconfig.gaggimate.defaults for the T-RGB envs only. The 8 MB
# headless env runs on a Seeed XIAO ESP32-S3 whose flash was not measured, so
# it keeps the inherited default.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_QIO=y
